  "prefLabel": "Ncr 565.03 Training Required for Initial Appointment of Forest Fire Wardens",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ncr 565.03 Training Required for Initial Appointment of Forest Fire Wardens. Unless already completed, a course of training consistent with the National Wildfire Coordinating Group (NWCG) S-130, Firefighting Training, shall be required within the initial 3-year term of the appointment for every forest fire warden. The training shall contain content approved by the division for the purposes of training basic wildland firefighting skills to the agent and shall be completed either in person, virtual, or through a combined format approved by the division, and as provided by the NWCG. The student receives a certificate upon course completion.\n\nSource. #14452, eff 12-6-25, EXPIRES 12-6-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ncr520-590.html"
